<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42105" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπῴχᾰτο</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		3pl.
		plpf.
		
			Pass.
		, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾶσαι γὰρ [πύλαι]
		ἐπῴχατο</span> all <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>were
				shut to,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				12.340
			</span></i> (= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπικεκλιμέναι ἦσαν,
				ἐπέκειντο,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Aristarch.
			</span></i>, who derived it from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐποίγω,</span> prob. rightly, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσοίγνυμι</span>; 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπωχλισμέναι ἦσαν</span>
			
			<i>were bolted,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Apollon.
				<u>Lex.</u>
			</span></i>, reading <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπώχατο</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάσας γὰρ ἐπῴχετο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Zenod.
				</span></i>
			, vulg.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
